        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-devaluation",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · devaluation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In nineteen eighty-five, the biggest economies even teamed up to push the dollar down together.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "1985",
          "label": "the Plaza Accord",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "bill"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "When everyone does it at once, it tips into a currency war.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-currencywar",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · currency war"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It traces back to an old idea. Sell more than you buy, whatever it takes.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Export at all costs",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That instinct is pure mercantilism, maximize exports and minimize imports.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-mercantilism",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · mercantilism"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In almost every single case, the goal was the same, protect local factories and jobs by selling more cheaply abroad.",
